e global uniqueness).\\\\\\\\n*   **Purpose:** This bucket will serve as the designated drop-off point for non-technical users to upload their news articles.\\\\\\\\n*   **Configuration:**\\\\\\\\n    *   **Access Control:** All public access will be blocked. Access will be granted exclusively to authorized IAM users/roles (e.g., the user managing content) and the processing Lambda function.\\\\\\\\n    *   **Event Notifications:** An event notification will be configured to trigger the `ProcessNewsArticle` Lambda function.\\\\\\\\n    *   **File Format:** Users will upload files in `.md` (Markdown) or `.txt` (plain text) format. The first line of the file will be treated as the article's title, and the remaining content will form the body of the article.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**2. S3 Event Notification**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Source Bucket:** `hoa-news-uploads-bucket`.\\\\\\\\n*   **Event Type:** `s3:ObjectCreated:*` - This will trigger the Lambda function whenever any new object is successfully uploaded to the bucket.\\\\\\\\n*   **Filtering (Recommended):** To prevent accidental triggers, a filter will be applied to the notification, restricting it to files with a `.txt` or `.md` suffix.\\\\\\\\n*   **Destination:** The notification will target the ARN of the `ProcessNewsArticle` Lambda function. The necessary permissions for S3 to invoke this Lambda function will be automatically configured as part of the notification setup.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**3. Lambda Function Logic**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*   **Function Name (Proposed):** `ProcessNewsArticleFunction`.\\\\\\\\n*   **Runtime:** Python 3.11.\\\\\\\\n*   **Core Logic:**\\\\\\\\n    1.  The function is triggered by the S3 event, receiving the bucket name and object key (file name) in the event payload.\\\\\\\\n    2.  Using the AWS SDK (Boto3), it will execute an `s3:GetObject` call to retrieve the uploaded file's content.\\\\\\\\n    3.  The file content will be parsed:\\\\\\\\n        *   **Title:** The first line of the